 Input and Generated Files
 &lt;a href="#input-and-generated-files" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A project normally contains these inputs:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Building AOSP</title><link>https://example.org/building-aosp/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Apr 2022 23:20:26 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/building-aosp/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;An Android Open Source Project checkout and its build artifacts require substantial
disk space; the exact requirement depends on the branch, target, and enabled variants.
Use a 64-bit Linux host with ample RAM, fast storage, and enough free space for both
the checkout and the output directory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="obtaining-the-source"&gt;
 Obtaining the Source
 &lt;a href="#obtaining-the-source" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;AOSP is distributed across many Git repositories. The &lt;code&gt;repo&lt;/code&gt; tool coordinates those
repositories from a manifest; it is a Python wrapper around Git rather than a source
control system of its own. Initialize the required branch with &lt;code&gt;repo init&lt;/code&gt;, then use
&lt;code&gt;repo sync&lt;/code&gt; to populate or update the checkout.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>